Docker with GitHub Actions

Today I learned how GitHub Actions integrates with Docker to automate container build and delivery.

🔹 Build Docker Images
Workflows can:
Build Docker images automatically
Use Dockerfiles in repositories
Ensure consistent builds
This enables containerized CI/CD.

🔹 Tag Images
Image tagging helps:
Track versions
Identify builds
Support rollbacks
Tags are critical for deployments.

🔹 Push to Registry
Built images can be pushed to:
Docker Hub
Amazon ECR
Other container registries
Secure authentication is required.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Automation builds images.
 Tags manage versions.
 Registries deliver containers.
